#: rust/rexon-core/src/de_customization.rs
msgid ""
"Pantheon's own settings service puts the elementary style back over the GTK "
"theme: at every login, whenever you change the accent color and — with the "
"automatic accent — whenever the wallpaper changes. Until then your theme "
"stays."
msgstr ""

#: rust/rexon-core/src/de_customization.rs
msgid ""
"Event sounds are played by a notification daemon (swaync, mako, dunst) or by "
"the app itself, not by the desktop shell. On tiling compositors you start "
"that daemon yourself — until you do, the theme stays silent."
msgstr ""

#: rust/rexon-core/src/de_customization.rs
msgid ""
"Every Qt app (VLC, qBittorrent, Krita, OBS) will pick the theme up. This "
"desktop has no Qt style switch of its own, so Rexon sets one up for you — "
"but the change only shows up after your next login."
msgstr ""

#: rust/rexon-core/src/de_customization.rs
msgid ""
"Live wallpapers work in the Pantheon “Classic Session” (X11). In the “Secure "
"Session” (Wayland) the Gala window manager doesn't let other programs draw "
"the desktop background, so only a still picture can be set there."
msgstr ""

#: rust/rexon-core/src/de_customization.rs
msgid ""
"A global theme is a Plasma package. Here Rexon applies its parts one by one "
"— colors, application style, icons, pointers, fonts and title bar buttons; "
"the window that opens before applying says what carries over."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Outside Plasma: the Color Schemes section note (GTK apps can't see KDE color schemes).
#: rust/rexon-core/src/de_customization.rs
msgid ""
"Outside Plasma, Rexon passes the scheme to KDE apps (Dolphin, Kate, Okular) "
"and to the other Qt apps — some of them only pick it up after your next "
"login. GTK apps (Firefox, GIMP) and most of the desktop's own apps don't "
"read KDE color schemes and keep their own colors — for GTK apps, pick a "
"matching theme in “GTK Themes”."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Why the Kvantum / Application Style sections are missing in Deepin.
#: rust/rexon-core/src/de_customization.rs
msgid ""
"Deepin's own apps (Control Center, file manager and the rest) draw "
"themselves with Deepin's Chameleon style. Switching the Qt style for the "
"whole session would take it away from them and break their look, so in "
"Deepin Rexon leaves the Qt style alone."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Why the Color Schemes section is missing in Deepin.
#: rust/rexon-core/src/de_customization.rs
msgid ""
"Deepin colors its apps itself, with its Chameleon style and its own accent "
"color in the Control Center. A KDE color scheme would only reach a few KDE "
"apps and leave the rest of the desktop mismatched, so in Deepin Rexon leaves "
"the colors to Deepin."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Why the Metacity/Marco and xfwm4 window border sections are missing in Cinnamon. “GTK Themes” is the Rexon section name, “Applications” the item in Cinnamon's own Themes settings.
#: rust/rexon-core/src/de_customization.rs
msgid ""
"In Cinnamon, window borders come from the GTK theme: since Cinnamon 5.4 its "
"window manager Muffin no longer loads separate border themes (Metacity, "
"Marco, xfwm4). To change the borders, pick a theme in “GTK Themes” — it's "
"the same as “Applications” in Cinnamon's own Themes settings."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: %1 is a list of desktops, %2 the desktop selected now.
#: rust/rexon-core/src/de_customization.rs
msgid ""
"This kind of customization only exists in: %1.\n"
"Your selected desktop is %2, where it simply does nothing, so we don't offer "
"it."
msgstr ""

